        "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-md",
        "max_width_desktop": "109ch",
        "richtext": "<p>¹ Based on removal testing of PM 2.5 (0.1 - 2.5 microns) and germs (H1N1, E.coli) up to 90min in a 30m3 room. Performance may vary. Not all Blueair air purifiers have been tested against SARS-CoV-2, and Blueair does not claim to kill\/prevent transmission of COVID-19.<\/p><p>² Comparing CADR performance of Blueair models with mechanical and electrostatic filtration vs same models with only H13 HEPA mechanical filtration.<\/p><p>³ When similar CADR was measured, Blueair models with mechanical and electrostatic filtration achieved less noise with less energy than same models with only H13 HEPA mechanical filtration. Noise refers to the dB(A) difference in acoustic power. Sound pressure measured on low fan speed.<\/p><p>⁴ Energy consumption on high fan speed. Compared to over 900 lumens incandescent light bulb.<\/p>",
        "richtext_style": "p2"
      }
    }
